{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Build the cinema seat-booking web application described in `spec/README.md`, as the React application already scaffolded in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in `apps/cinescope`); its stack is described in `spec/stack.md`. The work is split into tickets in `spec/tickets/`, to be implemented in order (01 movie list → 02 auditorium map → 03 seat selection → 04 booking/summary → 05 checkout → 06 confirmation → 07 final pass). `spec/README.md` is the complete specification: no questions should be asked, and where it is silent I must choose the simplest option that satisfies it. The task is finished only when every ticket's checkboxes are satisfied and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds. Standard repo-wide engineering instructions apply (no comments unless non-obvious, no unnecessary abstractions, confirm before risky/destructive actions, etc.), plus a git commit attribution instruction (append `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>` to commits and the PR-description footer to PRs) — not yet relevant since no commits have been requested or made.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Nx 23 monorepo, Vite build tool, React 19.3.0, React Router 6 (`BrowserRouter`), SCSS (CSS Modules supported via `@nx/react/typings/cssmodule.d.ts`), Vitest, ESLint flat config.\n   - MUI 9.4.0 (`@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`) + MUI X Date Pickers 9.14.0 with `dayjs` 1.11.23; `ThemeProvider`/`CssBaseline`/`LocalizationProvider` already wired in `main.tsx` (not modified).\n   - `json-server` 0.17.4 backend serving `db.json` at `http://localhost:3000` (movies/screenings/reservations endpoints); never edit `db.json` by hand.\n   - `sessionStorage`-backed booking state machine with strict per-route entry guards (not continuously re-checked while on a screen).\n   - Toast system: single visible toast, 4-second auto-dismiss, replaced (not queued) by new toasts.\n   - CSS Grid-based auditorium rendering: 28 implicit column tracks per row (4 + 2-aisle + 16 + 2-aisle + 4), using `grid-column: span N` for entrance/aisle/couch cells so auto-placement handles global column alignment without manual index math.\n   - Strict `data-testid` / `data-*` attribute contract (section 9 of spec) — verified empirically that TypeScript permits `data-*` attributes directly on MUI component props (Button, TextField, Checkbox, DatePicker, FormControlLabel, SnackbarContent) with no type errors.\n   - TypeScript `strict: true`; ESLint via Nx flat config (`@nx/eslint-plugin`, react-hooks exhaustive-deps rule, `@typescript-eslint/no-non-null-assertion` warning rule encountered and fixed).\n   - `pnpm` only (never npm/yarn); `CI=true` env var needed to avoid interactive TTY prompts when Nx/pnpm wants to reinstall `node_modules`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (all under `/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/` unless noted):\n\n   - **`api/types.ts`** (created): `Movie`, `Screening`, `ReservationCustomer`, `Reservation`, `CreateReservationPayload` interfaces matching spec section 2.1 exactly.\n\n   - **`api/client.ts`** (created): `BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:3000'`; generic `getJson<T>(path)` helper throwing on non-ok responses; exports `fetchMovies()`, `fetchScreeningsByDate(date)`, `fetchScreening(id)`, `fetchMovie(id)`, `createReservation(payload)` (POST with `Content-Type: application/json`, throws on non-ok).\n\n   - **`domain/dateFormat.ts`** (created): `ISO_DATE_FORMAT = 'YYYY-MM-DD'`; `today()`, `toIsoDate(date)`, `isValidIsoDate(value)` (regex + dayjs round-trip check, no customParseFormat plugin needed), `isPastDate(isoDate)`, `resolveSelectedDate(param)` (missing/invalid/past date → today's ISO date), `formatShowDate(isoDate, time)` using `dayjs(\\`${isoDate}T${time}\\`).format('dddd D MMM HH:mm')`.\n\n   - **`domain/seatLayout.ts`** (created, then edited twice for fixes): Constants `TOTAL_ROWS=15`, `COUCH_ROW=15`, `COUCH_PRICE=89`; `SeatState` type (`'available'|'selected'|'unavailable'|'accessible'`); `STATE_COLORS` record (`available:'#2E7D32'`, `selected:'#F9A825'`, `unavailable:'#C62828'`, `accessible:'#1565C0'`); `LEGEND_ITEMS` array; `seatId(row,col)`, `parseSeatId(id)`, `isAccessibleSeat(row,col)` (row===1 && col 10-15), `priceForRow(row)` (1-5→25, 6-10→32, 11-14→39, else throws), `formatPrice(price)`; `LayoutCell` discriminated union (`entrance`/`aisle`/`seat`/`couch`); `blockCells(row,start,end)` and `getRowCells(row)` generating the 28-track ordered layout (fixed via explicit spread instead of `.flat()` to preserve union typing):\n     ```ts\n     export function getRowCells(row: number): LayoutCell[] {\n       const left: LayoutCell[] = row <= 10 ? [{ type: 'entrance' }] : blockCells(row, 1, 4);\n       const aisle: LayoutCell = { type: 'aisle' };\n       return [...left, aisle, ...blockCells(row, 5, 20), aisle, ...blockCells(row, 21, 24)];\n     }\n     ```\n     `getSeatState()`/`getCouchState()`; `BookedItem` interface and `buildBookedItems(seatIds)` (groups/sorts by row then column, pairs row-15 columns into couches) — fixed to remove a non-null-assertion lint warning by iterating `columnsByRow.entries()` directly:\n     ```ts\n     const entries = [...columnsByRow.entries()].sort(([rowA], [rowB]) => rowA - rowB);\n     for (const [row, rawColumns] of entries) {\n       const columns = [...rawColumns].sort((a, b) => a - b);\n       ...\n     }\n     ```\n     `SelectedSeatsRow` interface and `buildSelectedSeatsRows(seatIds)` (reduces `buildBookedItems` output into `Row <r>: <seats>` display lines).\n\n   - **`domain/validation.ts`** (created): `EMAIL_RE = /^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/`, `PHONE_RE = /^\\d{9}$/`; `CheckoutErrors` interface; `validateCheckout(form: BookingForm): CheckoutErrors` implementing all spec 7 rules (empty→\"is required\" messages vs. rule-violation messages, phone optional, terms boolean check); `hasCheckoutErrors(errors)`.\n\n   - **`booking/types.ts`** (created): `BookingForm` interface (firstName, lastName, email, confirmEmail, phone, terms), `Booking` interface (screeningId, seats, form, paid, customerEmail), `EMPTY_BOOKING_FORM`, `createEmptyBooking(screeningId)`, `isBookingUsable(booking, screeningId)` (not null, !paid, matching screeningId, seats.length > 0).\n\n   - **`booking/BookingContext.tsx`** (created): `STORAGE_KEY = 'cinescope.booking'`; `loadBooking()`/`saveBooking()` sessionStorage helpers; `BookingProvider` component holding `booking` state (lazy-initialized from storage), persisting via `useEffect` on every change; exposes `startBookingForScreening`, `toggleSeatGroup` (returns `'added'|'removed'|'limit'`, enforces 10-seat cap, toggles ids as an atomic group), `removeSeats`, `updateForm`, `markPaid`, `clearBooking`; `useBooking()` hook throwing if used outside provider.\n\n   - **`toast/ToastContext.tsx`** (created): `ToastProvider` using MUI `Snackbar`+`SnackbarContent` (`data-testid=\"toast\"` on `SnackbarContent`), `{id, message}` state with a 4000ms `setTimeout` reset on every new `showToast()` call (even same text, via `Date.now()` id); `useToast()` hook.\n\n   - **`app/app.tsx`** (rewritten from scaffold): Wraps `<Routes>` in `ToastProvider` → `BookingProvider`, defines all 5 routes plus `<Route path=\"*\" element={<Navigate to=\"/\" replace />} />`.\n\n   - **`pages/movie-list/MovieListPage.module.scss`** and **`MovieListPage.tsx`** (created): Day picker (5 buttons via `dayButtons()` helper: `Today` + 4 weekday names) plus MUI `DatePicker` (`minDate={today()}`), URL state via `useSearchParams`/`resolveSelectedDate`; `LoadState` union (`loading`/`error`/`loaded`) fetching via `Promise.all([fetchMovies(), fetchScreeningsByDate(selectedDate)])`; `MovieCards` sub-component filtering/sorting screenings per movie; all section 9.1 testids applied including `data-date`/`data-selected` on day buttons and `data-movie-id`/`data-screening-id` on cards/buttons.\n\n   - **`pages/seat-selection/SeatMap.module.scss`**, **`SeatMap.tsx`**, **`Legend.module.scss`**, **`Legend.tsx`**, **`SelectedSeatsPanel.module.scss`**, **`SelectedSeatsPanel.tsx`**, **`SeatSelectionPage.module.scss`**, **`SeatSelectionPage.tsx`** (all created): `SeatMap` renders 15 `seat-row`s via CSS Grid (`grid-template-columns: repeat(28, 26px)`), each containing `row-label-left`/cells (`entrance` div with no testid, `aisle`, `seat` with `data-row`/`data-column`/`data-state`, `couch` with `data-row`/`data-column-start`/`data-column-end`/`data-state`)/`row-label-right`; `Legend` renders 4 `legend-item`s from `LEGEND_ITEMS`; `SelectedSeatsPanel` renders `selected-seats-count` + `selected-seats-row`s from `buildSelectedSeatsRows`; `SeatSelectionPage` fetches screening+movie in a mount effect (`[screeningId]` dep, eslint-disabled for exhaustive-deps on the full effect), calls `startBookingForScreening(screeningId)` only after successful load, redirects to `/` on any fetch failure, renders spec-ordered sections (title/subtitle/seat-limit-info/screen-indicator+SeatMap/Legend/SelectedSeatsPanel/Cancel+Continue), wires `handleToggle(ids)` → `toggleSeatGroup` → toast on `'limit'`.\n\n   - **`pages/summary/SummaryPage.module.scss`** and **`SummaryPage.tsx`** (created, one follow-up edit): Guard effect combining `isBookingUsable` check (immediate redirect) with screening/movie fetch (redirect on failure); render guard was tightened from `if (state.status === 'loading' || !booking)` to:\n     ```ts\n     if (state.status === 'loading' || !booking || !isBookingUsable(booking, screeningId)) {\n       return null;\n     }\n     ```\n     Renders `summary-title`, `summary-list`/`summary-item`s (title/datetime/row/seat/price/remove-button), `summary-total`, `back-button`/`confirm-button`; `handleRemove(item)` calls `removeSeats(item.ids)` and navigates to seat map if `items.length === 1` (last item).\n\n   - **`pages/checkout/CheckoutPage.module.scss`** and **`CheckoutPage.tsx`** (created): `TextFieldKey` union + `FIELD_TEST_ID`/`FIELD_LABEL` records; `Touched` type and `INITIAL_TOUCHED`; guard effect + render guard via `isBookingUsable` (no network fetch, since checkout only needs `booking.seats` for pricing); `renderField(field)` helper rendering `InputLabel`+`TextField`+conditional `FormHelperText`; terms row via `FormControlLabel`+`Checkbox` with its own conditional `FormHelperText`; `handlePay()` validates, marks all touched + toasts \"The form contains errors\" if invalid, else POSTs via `createReservation` (seats = `items.flatMap(i => i.ids)` in summary order, customer from form, totalPrice = summed item prices), `markPaid(form.email)` + navigate to `/confirmation` on success, re-enable + toast \"Payment failed. Please try again.\" on failure; Pay button text `Pay ${total.toFixed(2)} PLN` / `Processing…` while `submitting`, `disabled={submitting}`.\n\n   - **`pages/confirmation/ConfirmationPage.module.scss`** and **`ConfirmationPage.tsx`** (created): Guard effect/render guard via `!booking || !booking.paid`; renders `confirmation-heading`, `confirmation-message` (with `booking.customerEmail`), `confirmation-continue-button` (clears booking, navigates to `/`).\n\n   - **`apps/cinescope/src/mui-check.tsx`** (scratch file, created then deleted): Used only to empirically verify that `data-testid` typechecks directly on MUI `Button`/`TextField`/`Checkbox`/`DatePicker` components — confirmed no errors, then removed.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **pnpm/Nx no-TTY install prompt**: `pnpm nx show project cinescope --web=false` initially failed with `[ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY]`. Fixed by prefixing commands with `CI=true` (e.g. `CI=true pnpm nx show project cinescope --web=false`), which allowed the non-interactive `node_modules` reinstall to proceed successfully.\n   - **TS error in `seatLayout.ts`**: `getRowCells` originally built the array via `[left, [{type:'aisle'}], ...].flat()`, which widened to `(LayoutCell | {type: string})[]`, causing `Type '{ type: string; }' is not assignable to type 'LayoutCell'`. Fixed by replacing with explicit spreads and a typed `aisle: LayoutCell` constant (see code above) — confirmed via `npx tsc --noEmit -p apps/cinescope/tsconfig.app.json` with zero errors afterward.\n   - **ESLint warning in `seatLayout.ts`**: `@typescript-eslint/no-non-null-assertion` on `columnsByRow.get(row)!` inside `buildBookedItems`. Fixed by iterating `columnsByRow.entries()` directly instead of iterating sorted row keys and re-looking-up via `.get(row)!` (see code above). Re-ran `CI=true pnpm nx lint cinescope` — zero problems afterward.\n   - **Uncertainty about MUI + `data-testid` TypeScript compatibility**: Resolved by writing and typechecking a scratch file (`mui-check.tsx`) rather than guessing from reading `.d.ts` files (which showed no explicit `data-${string}` index signatures in MUI's own prop types) — confirmed TypeScript's JSX attribute checker permits `data-*`/`aria-*` attributes regardless of whether the target is an intrinsic DOM element or a custom component, so no wrapper-div workaround was needed.\n   - **Backend/dev-server connectivity confusion during manual verification** (not a code bug): Running `pnpm api` via a plain backgrounded subshell (`(pnpm api > /tmp/api.log 2>&1 &)`) appeared to not be reachable via `fetch('http://localhost:3000/...')` or `curl`-equivalent `/dev/tcp/127.0.0.1/3000` checks (\"fetch failed\" / \"Connection refused\"), even though a later `pnpm nx` background-task attempt hit `EADDRINUSE` on `::1:3000`, proving a server WAS running. Diagnosed via `exec 3<>/dev/tcp/::1/3000` (succeeded) and `fetch('http://[::1]:3000/movies')` (succeeded, returned real movie JSON, and `/tmp/api.log` showed `GET /movies 200`) that the json-server process was listening only on the IPv6 loopback address `::1`, not `127.0.0.1`, which was the actual cause of my own manual Node-fetch checks failing against `127.0.0.1`/plain `localhost`. This was a sandbox/tooling artifact of my own verification approach, not an application defect — the app's own `fetch('http://localhost:3000/...')` calls will be exercised by the real browser during the `run` skill's verification instead. `curl` is not installed in this environment (`/bin/bash: line 1: curl: command not found`), so raw `/dev/tcp` and Node `fetch` were used instead for manual checks.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Designed and implemented the full booking state machine (session-storage-backed, context-based) satisfying all of spec section 3.1's route-guard table and \"in progress until paid\" semantics, including the specific requirement that opening the seat map discards a stale/paid/mismatched booking only *after* the screening successfully loads, and that summary/checkout/confirmation guards run once on route entry rather than reactively.\n   - Designed the auditorium geometry purely algorithmically (no hardcoded per-row seat lists) via `getRowCells`, verified by derivation that it yields exactly 296 regular seats + 12 couches = 308 selectable elements as required by AC-15 (200 in rows 1-10, 96 in rows 11-14, 12 couches in row 15).\n   - Confirmed via empirical TypeScript scratch-testing (rather than assumption) that MUI components accept `data-testid` props directly, avoiding unnecessary wrapper-div indirection that could have complicated the DOM structure relative to the section 9.7 contract.\n   - Successfully got `pnpm nx build cinescope`, `pnpm nx lint cinescope`, and `npx tsc --noEmit -p apps/cinescope/tsconfig.app.json` all passing cleanly after the two fixes above — this satisfies the hard completion criterion \"`pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds\" at least for the current implementation state, though the full ticket checklist (all ACs) has not yet been manually/visually verified end-to-end.\n   - Started both the backend (`pnpm api`